Name: CLAS_2026_I0000000
Year: 2026
Summary: Single charged pion production C(e,e'p pi-) and C(e,e'p pi+) at 1.159, 2.257 and 4.453 GeV (e4nu)
Experiment: CLAS
Collider: CEBAF
InspireID: 0000000
Status: UNVALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
 - Julia Tena-Vidal <jtenavidal@gmail.com>
References:
 - 'CLAS and e4nu Collaborations, to be published'
RunInfo: Electron scattering on a $^{12}$C target at rest, at a beam energy of 1.159, 2.257 or 4.453 GeV.
  One run per beam energy; the histograms of the other two energies stay empty.
  The cross section of the run must be per carbon nucleus.
# The target is not always flagged as a beam particle (NuHepMC: status 11), so any second beam is
# accepted; the analysis checks the electron energy and the 12C target itself.
Beams: [e-, '*']
Description:
  'Differential cross sections for electron scattering on carbon with exactly one proton and one
  charged pion ($\pi^-$ or $\pi^+$) detected in the final state, as a function of the reconstructed
  hadronic invariant mass $W$ and of the calorimetric energy $E_{cal}$, at beam energies of 1.159,
  2.257 and 4.453 GeV, measured with the CLAS detector (e4nu). The data are corrected for detector
  acceptance and radiative effects. To compare a model with the data, the momenta of the generated
  final-state particles are smeared with the CLAS momentum resolutions, and the CLAS momentum and
  polar-angle thresholds are applied to the electron and to the hadrons. Events must have
  $Q^2$ above 0.1, 0.4 and 0.8 GeV$^2$ at 1.159, 2.257 and 4.453 GeV, exactly one detected proton,
  exactly one detected charged pion and no detected photon.'
ValidationInfo:
  'Validated against the previous ROOT-based e4nu comparison code with GENIE and Achilles NuHepMC samples:
  the integrated cross sections agree within statistics.'
Keywords: [electron scattering, pion production, nuclear]
